  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Thursday)\nIssued at 1132 AM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nEven cooler temperatures are expected on Saturday morning with\ngood radiational cooling, lighter winds and lower dewpoints, so\nanother freeze is expected likely including areas farther south\nthan who will see freezing temperatures Friday morning.\n\nThe surface ridge moves east Saturday with surface winds becoming\nsoutheasterly again. A storm system approaches the area this\nweekend with rain moving into the area on Saturday night and\npersisting into Sunday evening. This storm moves east of the area\nand an upper ridge establishes itself from south Texas towards the\nOzarks Tuesday/Wednesday. Although a southerly component of the\nsurface winds return and temperatures start a warming trend, the\narea is still under the influence of the large post-frontal\nsurface high keeping forecast high temperatures mid-week close to\nseasonal normals. Another shortwave in southwesterly flow looks to\napproach later in the week that could bring additional \nprecipitation chances Wednesday night into Thursday, although the\nmedium range models show variability on how strong this wave will\nbe.",
